DESCRIPTION Discovery band: DaemonSet desired-vs-ready-vs-available reasoning across nodes.

DEFINE CONST QUESTION AS "List the DaemonSets and confirm each is scheduled on all the nodes it should cover."
DEFINE CONST MAX_DURATION AS 480 seconds

ASSERT(POST to discussion endpoint returns 200 with conversationId)
ASSERT(SSE stream emits "thread_found" event within 30 seconds)
ASSERT(discussion completes with "done" event within MAX_DURATION)

ASSERT(at least 1 specialist contributes with signal=agree)
ASSERT(coordinator produces synthesis)
ASSERT(synthesis is non-empty)

# Deterministic, drift-tolerant guard: the cilium DaemonSet is permanent (its coverage is graded live by the reference); requiring >=5 DS-name lines tolerates add/remove churn.
ASSERT(synthesis CONTAINS "cilium")
ASSERT(synthesis matches "[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*" at least 5 times)

# Reference-grounded quality: the deferred LLM judge (kubemoot-fitness crew) scores
# the synthesis against this ground truth on method and honesty, not specific values.
ASSERT(DEFER synthesis REFLECTS "Enumerates DaemonSets and compares desired vs ready and available across nodes, noting any with unscheduled or unavailable pods. Coverage is graded against the live DaemonSet status at the time of the question: a DaemonSet whose ready count is below its desired count (because a node is cordoned, NotReady or tainted, or a pod is Pending or crashing) is correctly reported with its real desired and ready counts and the cause the live data shows; a DaemonSet that is fully scheduled is correctly reported as covered. The real DaemonSets are those the live listing shows: typically the Cilium CNI (cilium, cilium-envoy), the GPU-operator node set (nvidia device-plugin, feature-discovery, operator-validator), the democratic-csi node plugin, and the observability node agents (prometheus node-exporter, otel-collector, and the GPU-node dcgm-exporter). The CNI is Cilium: there is NO calico, NO kube-proxy DaemonSet (Cilium replaces kube-proxy), NO flannel or weave, and NO fluentd or fluent-bit (node logging runs through the otel-collector). A correct answer reports only DaemonSets present in the live listing with counts that match it; inventing calico, kube-proxy, fluentd, or any non-existent DaemonSet, or a desired or ready count that does not match the live status, is a fabrication to mark down.")
